            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Before the new one: say the Spanish for the tenant, then the Spanish for to rent."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: deshacer",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "deshacer — \"to undo; to unpack\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Deshago la maleta al llegar. I unpack my case when I arrive."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Conjugated like hacer: deshago, deshice. Deshacer la maleta — to unpack."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "deshacer is built on hacer \"to make, to do\" with des- \"un-\"; hacer is inherited from Latin facere."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for telling, explaining and describing at B1."
